  id: gpu
  displayName: Graphics Card (GPU)
  category: 4
  icon: {fileID: 0}
  mlLabel: gpu
  mlAliases: []
  specChips:
  - PCIe x16
  - 8-pin power
  - 650 W PSU
  shortDescription: Draws images, video and 3D graphics. Plugs into the PCIe x16
    slot and needs extra power.
  whatItDoes: The GPU has thousands of small cores that work in parallel, which is
    ideal for drawing frames in games and 3D apps.
  keyFacts:
  - Uses the top PCIe x16 slot
  - Needs an 8-pin PCIe power cable
  - Plug your monitor into the card, not the motherboard
  installationSteps:
  - Remove the expansion slot covers on the case.
  - Open the PCIe slot latch.
  - Press the card straight down until the latch clicks.
  - Screw the bracket to the case and connect PCIe power.
  safetyTip: Support long, heavy cards so they don't sag and stress the slot.
